      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "DEKLA DIVA (1) brings the most reliable recent profile, having been beaten just over a metre in NR 45 to 55 at Collie after starting a well-supported favourite, and she had already run second in Mares NR 40 to 55 at Wagin. She has recent head-to-head edges over IDEAL WHITBY and LIQUIDATOR, which strengthens the case. PACIFIC EAGLE (3) resumes from a first-up win in NR up to 44 at Collie and is proven at this track and distance, though the move to NR 45 to 53 makes this a sharper assignment. IDEAL WHITBY (8) was only beaten just over five metres in NR 45 to 55 at Collie and placed in NR 40 to 54 at Bunbury two back, so the form is sound despite the second-row query. FIVE STAR KEVIN (5) drops from NR 50 to 60 after a fair Collie fifth and has placed two times from three starts at this track and distance, giving him a place-to-winning hope if the class relief brings a lift.",
